6. Testing Phases

Testing activities are performed across different stages:

Pre-Production

- Pre-prod validation is performed before the application is released.
- Functional validations are performed against the pre-production build.

Production

- Application is deployed to production after completion of the required validations.

Post-Production / Post-Prod

- Post-production validations are performed after deployment is completed.
- These validations help ensure that the application is functioning correctly after the production deployment.

Smoke Testing

- Smoke testing is performed after the post-production deployment/validation activities.
- The purpose is to verify the critical functionality of the application after deployment.

